sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Pietak & Levin (2017) electrodiffusive Nernst-Planck gap-junction morphogen transport & cryptic two-headed memory — MorphoEval overall 91.5/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2017-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling.py` (91.7/100, up from 58.6/100 in Pass 1; +33.1 overall). The remediated script implements conservative Scharfetter-Gummel Nernst-Planck electrodiffusive transport of cationic serotonin (5-HT, z=+1) through symmetric Bell-form voltage-gated gap junctions coupled to the cAMP/PKA -> beta-catenin / ERK feedback loop, matching the exact analytical Boltzmann equilibrium ratio c_post/c_ant = exp(40/25.85) = 4.6992 (PDE = 4.6984, 9-point sweep r = 1.0000) and reproducing all 6 canonical regeneration phenotypes with zero head-count error (RMSE = 0.0000): Wild-Type `1H1T`, 8-Octanol pulse `2H0T`, Cryptic Washout Memory `2H0T` (persisting after eta_oct -> 0), SCH-28080/Forskolin `0H2T` headless, Uncharged Morphogen Control `z=0` (`2H0T`), and Targeted Posterior K+ Hyperpolarization Rescue `1H1T`, alongside automated bilateral ocelli segmentation on `planarian_ap_polarity_specimen.jpg` (N = 2 eyespots at x/L = 0.0528), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_082_bioelectric_morphogen_coupling.lean`. Overall 91.5/100 (faithfulness 91.5, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2017-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 556422 B, 2268×1863 px, artifact_sha256 13866bfc1f2741223e1a9f254b38f8424907b00fb5e328dc4576f885fdb242dc (sha256 13866bfc1f2741223e1a9f254b38f8424907b00fb5e328dc4576f885fdb242dc), spec_fingerprint d43466962273a22db00389bf276a7fa5ef9addd555b89cf3850d949e0d0823ee. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d43466962273a22db00389bf276a7fa5ef9addd555b89cf3850d949e0d0823ee; artifact_sha256: 13866bfc1f2741223e1a9f254b38f8424907b00fb5e328dc4576f885fdb242dc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling_reference.json=b118960086d59e02..., datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/paper_citations.bib=c446e775222f552c..., datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/planarian_ap_polarity_specimen.jpg=466029cc05610678..., datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/scout_manifest.json=bc8a4a2c8e734e1d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Pietak & Levin (2017) J. R. Soc. Interface 14:20170425 & Pietak & Levin (2016) Front. Bioeng. Biotechnol. 4:55 electrodiffusive Nernst-Planck transport of cationic serotonin (5-HT, z=+1) through voltage-gated gap junctions G_gj(DeltaV) | Boltzmann zero-flux equilibrium concentration ratio c_post/c_ant = exp(-(z*F/(R*T))*(V_post - V_ant)) = 4.70 under wild-type planarian AP polarization (-20 mV anterior vs -60 mV posterior) | Cyclic-AMP / PKA / beta-catenin / ERK mutual feedback loop and permanent cryptic two-headed (2H0T) planarian memory persistence after transient 8-octanol gap-junction blockade and washout (Durant et al. 2017); reconstructed_in_script: 1D Scharfetter-Gummel conservative Nernst-Planck electrodiffusive 5-HT + voltage-gated gap-junction + cAMP/PKA/beta-catenin/ERK PDE across 6 experimental regimes and 9-point Boltzmann voltage sweep | Automated dorsal body-contour and bilateral photoreceptor ocelli segmentation on planarian_ap_polarity_specimen.jpg (N=2 eyespots at x/L=0.0528, length=1478 px) and 2D body-plan silhouette synthesis; transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior electrodiffusive 5-HT, beta-catenin, and ERK profiles mapped onto 2D dorsal planarian body-plan silhouettes and eyespot coordinates; does_not_claim: Full 3D finite-volume Voronoi cell lattice geometry of BETSE or explicit sub-millisecond action potential spiking." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple intracellular Ca2+ and IP3 electrodiffusion alongside 5-HT to model heteromorphosis and stochastic 1H1T/2H0T bistable branching probabilities.",
            "remediation needed: Extend the 1D Scharfetter-Gummel Nernst-Planck solver to an irregular 2D Voronoi cell network matching the full BETSE tissue geometry." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.915"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

